1
00:00:00,111 --> 00:00:01,432
Welcome to Box Breathing.

2
00:00:02,133 --> 00:00:08,098
This is a simple breathing practice that can help your system slow down and find a steadier rhythm.

3
00:00:08,939 --> 00:00:19,288
We will breathe in for four counts, hold for four counts, breathe out for four counts, and hold again for four counts.

4
00:00:26,361 --> 00:00:33,243
If holding your breath does not feel good, you can simply breathe gently and skip the holds.

5
00:00:40,425 --> 00:00:42,666
Let this practice be flexible.

6
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:48,528
Begin by settling into a comfortable position.

7
00:00:49,653 --> 00:00:52,154
Let your shoulders soften if they can.

8
00:00:53,354 --> 00:00:54,754
Let your jaw loosen.

9
00:00:56,015 --> 00:00:57,275
Let your hands rest.

10
00:00:58,715 --> 00:01:02,436
Take one natural breath in and let it out.

11
00:01:03,417 --> 00:01:04,157
Now we'll begin.

12
00:01:05,197 --> 00:01:09,358
Breathe in one, two, three, four, hold one,

13
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:42,966
two three four breathe out one two three four hold one two

14
00:01:45,130 --> 00:01:50,455
Three, four, good, again, breathe in.

15
00:01:53,178 --> 00:01:59,504
One, two, three, four, hold.

16
00:02:02,263 --> 00:02:06,227
One, two, three, four.

17
00:02:07,128 --> 00:02:07,769
Breathe out.

18
00:02:08,610 --> 00:02:11,252
One, two, three, four.

19
00:02:12,433 --> 00:02:12,854
Hold.

20
00:02:14,355 --> 00:02:18,319
One, two, three, four.

21
00:02:19,761 --> 00:02:24,165
Let your body follow the rhythm as much as it wants to.

22
00:02:25,406 --> 00:02:26,147
Breathe in.

23
00:02:39,233 --> 00:02:42,476
One, two, three, four.

24
00:02:44,078 --> 00:02:44,418
Hold.

25
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:47,261
On.

26
00:02:47,581 --> 00:02:50,584
Two, three, four.

27
00:02:53,987 --> 00:02:54,727
Breathe out.

28
00:02:55,868 --> 00:02:59,492
One, two, three, four.

29
00:03:00,673 --> 00:03:01,033
Hold.

30
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:07,603
One, two, three, four.

31
00:03:08,544 --> 00:03:10,925
If your mind wanders, that is okay.

32
00:03:11,906 --> 00:03:13,467
Just come back to the next count.

33
00:03:14,508 --> 00:03:15,189
Breathe in.

34
00:03:16,570 --> 00:03:19,832
One, two, three, four.

35
00:03:22,454 --> 00:03:22,794
Hold.

36
00:03:25,456 --> 00:03:27,518
One, two, three, four.

37
00:03:32,136 --> 00:03:32,776
Breathe out.

38
00:03:33,637 --> 00:03:36,118
One, two, three, four.

39
00:03:37,298 --> 00:03:37,739
Hold.

40
00:03:48,283 --> 00:03:52,725
One, two, three, four.

41
00:03:53,586 --> 00:03:55,747
Now let the counting become softer.

42
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:58,408
Breathe in for four.

43
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,321
Hold for four.

44
00:04:10,264 --> 00:04:11,825
Breathe out for four.

45
00:04:12,725 --> 00:04:14,166
Hold for four.

46
00:04:19,129 --> 00:04:21,330
Again breathe in.

47
00:04:26,133 --> 00:04:26,594
Hold.

48
00:04:31,557 --> 00:04:32,437
Breathe out.

49
00:04:33,258 --> 00:04:33,598
Hold.

50
00:04:38,599 --> 00:04:46,228
Now release the counting, let your breathing return to whatever pace feels natural.

51
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,742
Notice your body.

52
00:05:10,688 --> 00:05:11,788
Notice your breath.

53
00:05:12,609 --> 00:05:16,770
Notice whether anything inside feels even slightly more settled.

54
00:05:17,910 --> 00:05:21,531
If parts of you still feel activated, that is okay.

55
00:05:22,552 --> 00:05:24,452
The goal is not to force calm.

56
00:05:25,253 --> 00:05:28,594
The goal is to offer your system a steady rhythm.

57
00:05:29,754 --> 00:05:34,655
Take one final breath in and let it out slowly.

58
00:05:35,496 --> 00:05:39,197
When you are ready, return your attention to the room around you.

59
00:05:40,497 --> 00:05:42,905
Let this rhythm be something you can come back to.

60
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:51,835
Not as a command to calm down, but as a steady square of support your body can lean on when it is ready.
